,"initials":"K","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1247-4265"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Metabolic Signaling, EPFL, 1015 Lausanne, Switzerland."}]}},{"fullName":"Menzies KJ","lastName":"Menzies","firstName":"Keir J","initials":"KJ","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1873-8500"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratory of Integrative and Systems Physiology, École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne (EPFL), 1015 Lausanne, Switzerland. Interdisciplinary School of Health Sciences, University of Ottawa Brain and Mind Research Institute, 451 Smyth Road, K1H 8M5 Ottawa, Ontario, Canada. kmenzies@uottawa.ca admin.auwerx@epfl.ch."}]}},{"fullName":"Auwerx J","lastName":"Auwerx","firstName":"Johan","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5065-5393"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratory of Integrative and Systems Physiology, École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne (EPFL), 1015 Lausanne, Switzerland. kmenzies@uottawa.ca admin.auwerx@epfl.ch."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5905-6760"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8089-4785"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1873-8500"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4081-5752"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5065-5393"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8256-3901"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8499-9514"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9267-8278"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1247-4265"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1655-9557"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","recommended_reviews","related_data","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"6292","volume":"352","journalIssueId":2420899,"dateOfPublication":"2016 Jun","monthOfPublication":6,"yearOfPublication":2016,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Science","title":"Science (New York, N.Y.)","essn":"1095-9203","issn":"0036-8075","isoabbreviation":"Science","nlmid":"0404511"},"printPublicationDate":"2016-06-01"},"pubYear":"2016","pageInfo":"1436-1443","abstractText":"Adult stem cells (SCs) are essential for tissue maintenance and regeneration yet are susceptible to senescence during aging. We demonstrate the importance of the amount of the oxidized form of cellular nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide (NAD(+)) and its effect on mitochondrial activity as a pivotal switch to modulate muscle SC (MuSC) senescence. Treatment with the NAD(+) precursor nicotinamide riboside (NR) induced the mitochondrial unfolded protein response and synthesis of prohibitin proteins, and this rejuvenated MuSCs in aged mice. NR also prevented MuSC senescence in the mdx (C57BL/10ScSn-Dmd(mdx)/J) mouse model of muscular dystrophy. We furthermore demonstrate that NR delays senescence of neural SCs and melanocyte SCs and increases mouse life span. Strategies that conserve cellular NAD(+) may reprogram dysfunctional SCs and improve life span in mammals.","affiliation":"Laboratory of Integrative and Systems Physiology, École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne (EPFL), 1015 Lausanne, Switzerland.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIA NIH HHS","acronym":"AG","grantId":"R01AG043930","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Swiss National Science Foundation","acronym":"SNSF_","grantId":"31003A-140780","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Systems X","grantId":"SySX.ch 2013/153","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Krebsforschung Schweiz/SwissCancerLeague","grantId":"KFS-3082-02-2013","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIH","grantId":"R01AG043930","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Heart and Stroke Foundation of Canada","orderIn":0},{"agency":"University of Ottawa","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mitochondria","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_